<title>ARGENTINA: ARGENTINE WEEKLY OFFICIAL CROP PROGRESS.</title>
<headline>ARGENTINE WEEKLY OFFICIAL CROP PROGRESS.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 74.1 percent of their 1997/98 wheat crop by Aug 1, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly report Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared with 89.9 percent completion of a larger sown area by the same date last season. Absence of rain allowed sowing to advance in previously wet areas. In Buenos Aires province farmers had sowed 60.7 percent of their intended area, leaving it still 28.3 percent behind the same stage a year ago. In Cordoba province, farmers had sowed 91.9 percent of their intended areas, in Entre Rios 98 percent and in La Pampa 89.3 percent.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Wheat     6,250  74.1  (89.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,952  100.0(100.0) 3,225.0   99.3  (98.7)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 6,346.9  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,936.2  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sorghum     805  100.0(100.0)   677.2   99.2  (99.4)</p>
